# Developer-stack configuration for compose.dev.yml.
#
# Copy this file to ".env" and adjust as needed:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# This file contains ONLY non-secret, non-deployment-specific configuration.
# NEVER put real API keys, n8n credentials, invoice data, or internal
# service addresses here or in ".env" if you intend to commit it -- ".env"
# is git-ignored precisely so local secrets never end up in version control.
# The default "docker compose -f compose.dev.yml up --build" start works
# with NO values set below: Flow 1a (structured invoices, no AI) works with
# zero external credentials, and Flow 1b stays visible but inactive/
# unconfigured until you deliberately opt into local or cloud AI.

# --- Optional: local AI for Flow 1b ("PDF with local AI") ------------------
#
# Points Flow 1b's local extraction lane at a local, OpenAI-compatible
# chat-completions endpoint you already run yourself (e.g. LM Studio,
# Ollama with an OpenAI-compatible proxy, or any self-hosted equivalent).
# This project does NOT bundle, download, or run a model for you -- there is
# no local-AI Compose service. Point this at your own already-running
# endpoint. Leaving it unset means the local AI lane reports
# nicht_pruefbar/technical_review ("AI_LOCAL_PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE") instead
# of silently falling back to cloud AI.
#
# Expect real hardware/download cost if you stand up a local multimodal
# model yourself: multi-GB weights and a GPU (or a slow CPU fallback) are
# typical for anything capable of reading an invoice PDF.
#
# LOCAL_LLM_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:1234/v1
# LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=your-local-model-name

# Most local OpenAI-compatible vision endpoints (verified against LM
# Studio) reject a raw PDF passed as an image_url part and need an actual
# rendered image -- unlike Gemini's cloud API, which accepts the PDF
# directly. Run examples/n8n/scripts/pdf_render_service.py yourself
# (requires `pip install pymupdf`) and point this at it. Only needed for
# the local lane.
# LOCAL_PDF_RENDER_URL=http://host.docker.internal:8098

# --- Cloud AI for Flow 1b ("PDF with cloud AI") -----------------------------
#
# There is no cloud-AI variable here on purpose: the Gemini credential is
# selected inside the n8n UI itself (Credentials -> Google Gemini (PaLM)
# API), never via an environment variable or the browser. See
# examples/n8n/README.md for the exact steps. Flow 1b stays inactive until
# you select a real credential there.
